# Warehouse camera recording (PrepCorex)

When the user asks about the **camera feature**, use this implementation as the current v1 baseline.

## Goal

Optional stage recording on warehouse phone → live client view (LiveKit) → local IndexedDB clip → confirmed upload to **admin Google Drive**, linked to inbound request or outbound shipment.

## Stages

- **Receive** (inbound): warehouse receiving page; client Inventory live banner + watch dialog
- **Pick / Pack / Dispatch** (outbound): optional recorder on each Ops screen; client **Shipped orders** watch dialog; clips share the same `shipmentRequestId`
- **Gallery**: Warehouse Ops → Camera gallery lists **this device’s** local clips (operator’s) for upload later or delete

## Agreed architecture

- **Camera:** selectable front/back phone or tablet browser camera
- **Recording:** MediaRecorder; pause/resume/stop; multiple clips per request/shipment stage
- **Local storage:** completed Blob in IndexedDB on the same phone/browser until upload/removal
- **Live:** same camera track publishes to managed LiveKit Cloud with short-lived server-issued tokens
- **Privacy:** client tokens work only for sessions whose `clientUserId` matches the signed-in user
- **Playback:** after Drive upload, clients watch through PrepCorex (`/playback`); no raw Drive link
- **Ended notice:** Inventory shows live-ended for **receive** product/SKU until dismissed
- **Cloud storage:** resumable direct browser upload to private admin Google Drive under
  `PrepCorex Warehouse Ops Recordings/{warehouse}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{DD}/{client}/{Inbound|Outbound…}/{stage YYYY-MM-DD}/`
- **Metadata:** server-only `warehouseCameraSessions` (`jobType`, `inventoryRequestIds` and/or `shipmentRequestIds`, Drive metadata)
- **Live relay:** Managed LiveKit Cloud + short-lived PrepCorex viewer tokens (not raw RTSP to browser)
- **Live state:** eight-second recorder heartbeat; client polling every five seconds; hide after stop or 30 seconds without heartbeat
- **Request context:** live client notices identify product, SKU, and inbound request ID (receive)

## Do not confuse with

- Existing barcode **scan camera** UI (`scan-camera-button`, etc.) — not video recording
- Receive **still photos** (Firebase Storage `warehouse-receive/…`)

